Do it yourself.

[[Enzo Mari]] got so frustrated that a piece of furniture he had designed to be great! — cheap, high quality, useful — was ignored by the market (my memory remembers the anecdote as being about a sofa that turns into a sleeper in an interesting way). This birthed the idea that perhaps furniture buyers don't really understand what makes a piece of furniture "good"

That led to the development of a series of furniture objects all designed to make them yourself from simple dimensional lumber and a hammer and nails.

